From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: HKCU\Keyboard Layout\Preload is the person's, never rewritten (9157)

Preload lists a person's keyboards in their order (Settings > Time &
Language > Language writes it, a keyboard of another language than theirs
as a "d00Nllll" substitute that Substitutes maps to its KLID; Setup and the
first-run setup write it for a new account). Windows writes it once, when
the profile is made, and nothing else ever rewrites it. Wine's
sysparams_init wrote "1" = the locale's layout at every process start: a
person whose first keyboard was German (or Dvorak, or any other language's)
had US English back as soon as any program ran -- and the console's
keyboard layout name (GetConsoleKeyboardLayoutName, 9711) with it.

Now "1" is written only when there is none (a new profile).

Gate test/kbdpreload-gate.sh. Mutant SG_MUTANT_KBD_PRELOAD_REWRITE.
---
 dlls/win32u/sysparams.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

--- a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -5835,6 +5835,23 @@ void sysparams_init(void)
     pthread_mutexattr_destroy( &attr );
 
     if ((hkey = reg_create_ascii_key( hkcu_key, "Keyboard Layout\\Preload", 0, NULL )))
+    {
+        char preload_buf[offsetof(KEY_VALUE_PARTIAL_INFORMATION, Data[KL_NAMELENGTH * sizeof(WCHAR)])];
+
+        /* Stained Glass OS (9157): Preload is the person's keyboards, in their order, as Settings writes
+         * them (a keyboard of another language than theirs through Substitutes): Windows' setup writes it
+         * once and nothing rewrites it. Every process start here made "1" the locale's layout -- the
+         * person's first keyboard became US English again whenever a program ran. Written only when
+         * there is none (a new profile). */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_KBD_PRELOAD_REWRITE
+        if (query_reg_ascii_value( hkey, "1", (KEY_VALUE_PARTIAL_INFORMATION *)preload_buf, sizeof(preload_buf) ))
+        {
+            NtClose( hkey );
+            hkey = 0;
+        }
+#endif
+    }
+    if (hkey)
     {
         BOOL got;
 
